 **Verification and computational scope:** The full **33-statement V2i Comparator suite** ended with `Lean default kernel accepts the solution` in the development container (13,997 s, replaying V2h's reused moments). The statement-level negative control (`genEntry_eq` with a doubled right side) was rejected. Of the eight Lean controls, four positive were accepted and four negative rejected. Monte Carlo at $N=44$ gave $z=0.52$, $0.38$ and $1.06$. The certificate build took 1,543 s (peak 3.89 GB). V2i proves the exact representation of every $B_{21}$ entry; evaluating further entries requires their moment tables. The $846\times846$ matrices, $P^\star$ and the variational certificate remain targets.
 
+## 13. Shared-moment aggregation of Gram entries (V2j)
+
+**Lean:** `Solution/MomentAgg.lean`, `Solution/MomentAggDemo1.lean` through `Solution/MomentAggDemo4.lean`, `Solution/MomentAggSuite.lean`  
+**Definitions:** `BGP212/MomentAgg.lean`  
+**Challenge and Comparator:** `Challenge/MomentAgg.lean`, `Comparator/moment_agg_v2j.json`  
+**Specification and generator:** `Exploratory/V2j/SPEC.md`, `specs/checks/moment_agg_v2j_demo.py`  
+**Result record:** `specs/results/V2j_moment_agg.yaml`
+
+**Linearity and locality.** V2i's piece value is linear in its moment oracle and reads it only at a computable, duplicate-free key list (`genPieceWith_listSum`, `genPieceWith_congr`). Hence, for any duplicate-free key list $S$ covering those keys,
+
+$$
+\texttt{genPieceWith}\,(\dots)\,M\,(\dots)=\sum_{s\in S}\texttt{genPieceWith}\,(\dots)\,\delta_s\,(\dots)\cdot M(s).
+$$
+
+**Aggregation.** For weighted generator pairs $w=(c,a_1,\lambda_1,a_2,\lambda_2)$, coefficients are collected per moment key across all pairs before any moment is evaluated. Then
+
+$$
+\sum_w c\,J_T[G_{a_1,\lambda_1},G_{a_2,\lambda_2}]=\texttt{aggEntryVal}\,N\,g\,L\,\tau\,C\,ws ,
+$$
+
+and each distinct moment is evaluated once per piece (`aggEntryVal_eq`, `jT_weighted_eq_agg`). This is the algebraic shape of $J_T(P^\star)=\sum_{i,j}c_ic_jJ_T[G_i,G_j]$.
+
+**Demonstration (kernel).** Piece $(6,3)$ of $J_T[P_2,P_2]$ at Table 3 is recomputed from 19 moments. V2i's direct form makes 115 oracle queries. The result proves exactly V2i's certified statement `gpPP_6_3`, now independent of V2h's moment lemmas. V2i's four entries on that piece come from 21 shared keys instead of 50. On synthetic data, $J_T[P_2,P_2]=0.00136761$ (V2h's value). Direct single-declaration kernel evaluation exhausts memory; the staged certificates complete in 90, 20, 4 and 81 s.
+
+**Scope:** V2j establishes the aggregation identities and the evaluation pattern. The symmetric-function reduction needed for many-part power-sum products, the $846\times846$ matrices, $P^\star$ and the variational certificate remain targets (`Exploratory/V2j/SPEC.md` §5–6).
+
 ## Formal verification and provenance
 
 - **Source:** [`thinkthoughts/lean-bgp212`](https://github.com/thinkthoughts/lean-bgp212)
